============================================================
00. ORIGINAL VISION AND DESIGN OBJECTIVES
============================================================

GammaThink is a neuro-symbolic AI architecture.

Its primary objective is NOT to build a conventional
large language model that performs all reasoning
inside neural-network inference.

Instead, GammaThink separates intelligence into
specialised components:

1. A neural language interpreter converts natural
   language into structured machine-readable intent.

2. A symbolic reasoning engine performs explicit,
   traceable reasoning over structured knowledge.

3. A persistent Chain of Knowledge (CoK) stores
   knowledge, derivations, evidence, assumptions,
   contradictions and reusable reasoning results.

4. A knowledge compiler converts external source
   material into candidate structured knowledge.

5. A distributed knowledge system allows approved,
   verified contributions to be shared between
   GammaThink instances.

6. A local conversational memory system preserves
   session context and historical information even
   when the neural interpreter is unloaded.

7. A human-facing interface allows users to inspect
   how conclusions were reached.

GammaThink should be capable of accumulating
structured knowledge without requiring the neural
interpreter to be retrained after every update.

Its architecture should support useful operation
on modest consumer hardware.

The intended long-term outcome is a system that
can reason over a growing body of knowledge,
reuse verified derivations, identify gaps in its
understanding and propose new hypotheses.

This is an architectural objective, not a claim
of achieved general intelligence.


