============================================================
06. THREE-LAYER LOCAL CONTEXT MEMORY
============================================================

PURPOSE:

Preserve conversational continuity and
project context independently of the
neural model's active context window.

The system uses three complementary layers.


LAYER 1: RECENT CONVERSATION
----------------------------

Stores a bounded window of recent
conversation messages in original form.

Includes:

- Latest user messages
- Latest assistant responses
- Recent clarifications
- Recent corrections
- Immediate dialogue references

This layer prioritises exact wording.

It is normally included automatically
in each new context package.

The window size is configurable.


LAYER 2: PERSISTENT SESSION SUMMARY
-----------------------------------

Stores a compact, structured record
of the active conversation.

Includes:

- Original session objective
- Current goals
- Important constraints
- Decisions already made
- Project requirements
- User corrections
- Unresolved questions
- Progress checkpoints
- Important references

This layer protects important context
from being lost when earlier messages
fall outside the recent-chat window.

The session summary is periodically
updated and versioned.

Original messages are never replaced
or destroyed by the summary.

Important constraints may be pinned
independently of summary compression.


LAYER 3: LONG-TERM LOCAL RAG
-----------------------------

Stores searchable historical context.

Includes:

- Older conversation messages
- Previous session summaries
- Project documentation
- Relevant local files
- Historical decisions
- User preferences
- Previous task results
- Persistent project notes

Retrieval may combine:

- SQLite FTS5
- Exact keyword matching
- Metadata filtering
- Session-aware filtering
- Recency weighting
- Optional vector embeddings
- Hybrid ranking

The retrieval engine selects relevant
excerpts rather than loading the entire
database into the model.


